    "font" : "Helvetica",
    "font size" : 9.96,
    "text color" : "[0.0]",
    "content" : "A thin-provisioned volume feature that is called zero detect provides clients with the ability to reclaim unused allocated disk space (zeros) when they are converting a fully allocated volume to a thin-provisioned volume by using volume mirroring."
  }, {
    "type" : "heading",
    "pdfua_tag" : "H1",
    "id" : 36,
    "level" : "Doctitle",
    "page number" : 1,
    "bounding box" : [ 63.333, 640.333, 303.667, 662.333 ],
    "heading level" : 1,
    "font" : "Helvetica-Bold",
    "font size" : 15.96,
    "text color" : "[0.0]",
    "content" : "3.12 Host attachment planning"
  }, {
    "type" : "paragraph",
    "pdfua_tag" : "P",
    "id" : 37,
    "page number" : 1,
    "bounding box" : [ 135.0, 567.0, 546.333, 628.333 ],
    "font" : "Helvetica",
    "font size" : 9.96,
    "text color" : "[0.0]",
    "content" : "The typical FC host attachment to the Storwize V7000 is done through SAN fabric. However, the system allows direct attachment connectivity between its 8 Gb or 16 Gb Fibre Channel ports and host ports. No special configuration is required for host systems that are using this configuration. However, the maximum number of directly attached hosts is severely limited by the number of FC ports on Storwize V7000’s nodes."
  }, {
    "type" : "paragraph",
    "pdfua_tag" : "P",
    "id" : 38,
    "page number" : 1,
    "bounding box" : [ 135.0, 497.0, 546.667, 559.667 ],
    "font" : "Helvetica",
    "font size" : 9.96,
    "text color" : "[0.0]",
    "content" : "The Storwize V7000 imposes no particular limit on the distance between the Storwize V7000 nodes and host servers. However, for host attachment, the Storwize V7000 supports up to three ISL hops in the fabric. This capacity means that the server to the Storwize V7000 can be separated by up to five FC links, four of which can be 10 km long (6.2 miles) if long wave Small Form-factor Pluggables (SFPs) are used."
  }, {
    "type" : "paragraph",
    "pdfua_tag" : "P",
    "id" : 39,
    "page number" : 1,
    "bounding box" : [ 135.0, 465.333, 547.0, 490.0 ],
    "font" : "Helvetica",
    "font size" : 9.96,
    "text color" : "[0.0]",
    "content" : "Figure 3-9 shows an example of a supported configuration with Storwize V7000 nodes using shortwave SFPs."
